</FIGURE>
<SPEC ID = "T120025K663K871X01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Cruising Range Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>0~999km</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The meter computer calculates the fuel consumption from the engine speed, fuel injection volume, etc., and calculates and displays the cruising range from the current fuel level signal.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>With the power source mode ON, the previous data is displayed.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, the display is blank (no display).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
